# Local secrets for `supabase functions serve --env-file supabase/.env`
# SUPABASE_URL and the service role key are injected automatically by the
# Supabase runtime — only add third-party secrets here (e.g. the teammate's
# Google Cloud ML service credentials, once known).

# weatherapi.com API key, used by supabase/functions/weather to look up
# outside temperature/humidity by location. Get one at https://www.weatherapi.com/
WEATHERAPI_KEY=

# GCP service account JSON key (single line), used by supabase/functions/occupancy-vision
# to call Vertex AI's generateContent for camera-based headcount estimation.
# The service account needs the "Vertex AI User" (roles/aiplatform.user) role.
# NOT the Gemini Developer API — that path was tried first but this project's GCP
# billing credit doesn't apply to the Gemini Developer API's prepay wallet, so
# occupancy-vision authenticates via Vertex AI + a service account instead (see
# CLAUDE.md's occupancy-vision section for the full story).
# Paste the downloaded key file's content compacted to one line, e.g.:
#   python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.dumps(json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))))" ~/Downloads/<key>.json
GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
